The packaging has no labels and is directly called to the supplier without any identification; they say it's genuine if there's doubt, and can send samples via courier for inspection at Johnson & Johnson Company; they also leave their license plate number and phone number behind, promising to send an SMS notification of my information being inputted into the Johnson & Johnson warranty card; but I haven't received any message yet?
The packaging is damaged. I'll wait for time to inspect the quality of the products.
The outer packaging is severely damaged; however, the inner box appears to be new, but the instruction manual seems not to be new. It was just renovated in September and I am stockpiling. I hope that it will not be bad when I get there. Please explain why so many customers have mentioned damage to the packaging while you seem to handle it calmly. Thank you!
